# Module security — endpoints & uploads

HTTP-callable module code must not run without authentication. Validate request **values** with `module-input.mdc`; escape for SQL with `module-sql.mdc`.

## Entrypoint guard

Every PHP file reachable from the web must start with:

```php
if (!defined('_PS_VERSION_')) {
    exit;
}
```

Cron scripts and includes loaded only from guarded parents may use the same check or `require` a parent that already defined `_PS_VERSION_`.

## AJAX & front actions — no external ajax files

Per [PrestaShop good practices](https://devdocs.prestashop-project.org/9/modules/creation/good-practices/): **do not** add standalone `ajax.php` (or similar) outside PrestaShop routing.

| Pattern | Use |
|---|---|
| Front-office AJAX | `ModuleFrontController` + `module` / `controller` query params |
| Back-office AJAX | `ModuleAdminController` or the module's existing admin controller pattern |
| Long-running cron URL | Dedicated controller or cron script with **token check at the top** |

Follow the **same token pattern** already used in the target module (`instant_token`, `verify_token`, `Tools::getAdminTokenLite`, etc.) — do not invent a second scheme in parallel.

```php
// ✅ GOOD — reject before any work (pattern varies per module; match neighbours)
$token = Tools::getValue('token');
if (!$token || $token !== Tools::getAdminTokenLite('AdminModules')) {
    exit;
}
```

## Token required

- **Cron URLs** and **background import/export URLs**: mandatory secret/token query param or admin session; return `403` / `exit` on mismatch.
- **Never** rely on obscurity (`/modules/foo/cron.php` with no check).
- Tokens in URLs must not be logged (see `module-logging.mdc`).

## File uploads

When the module accepts uploads:

1. Whitelist extensions and check MIME (`mime_content_type` or `finfo_file`) — do not trust `$_FILES['type']`.
2. Reject executable types (`.php`, `.phtml`, `.htaccess`, …).
3. Store under a module-owned directory from `module-paths.mdc`, not web-served paths unless strictly required.
4. Validate size limits before moving the file.

## Back-office assets

Load BO JavaScript/CSS only where needed — e.g. when `Tools::getValue('configure') === $this->name` in `hookDisplayBackOfficeHeader` (or the module's equivalent hook). Do not inject assets on every admin page.

## Never

- Standalone ajax endpoints bypassing PrestaShop bootstrap.
- Cron or import URLs without a token check.
- Saving uploads with the client-provided filename unchanged in a public directory.
